    description: "**Origin.** Filed 2026-05-30 as a sub-META of INV-fabov following the linked-pile L1 investigation. Sub-META C.\n\n**The shape.** Five active items describe \"value must be in a known registry but isn't checked.\" A CLI flag accepts arbitrary strings as the value of a flag whose semantics require a registry lookup (language catalog, framework catalog, section vocabulary, view vocabulary). When the string isn't a registry member, the subcommand proceeds (silently producing empty/wrong output) rather than rejecting with a helpful \"did you mean…\" hint.\n\n**Fix shape.** A shared argparse `choices=` wiring backed by the relevant catalog/registry, plus a small fuzzy-match helper for `--did-you-mean` suggestion text. Each member item is one subcommand × one registry binding.\n\n**Members (5).** INV-gufod (config silently accepts framework/linker names as if they were languages), INV-gapib (all --input consumers silently accept wrong-view JSON), INV-subak (config --format json: function_summaries empty for ALL 281 languages — the \"281\" is the silent-accept artifact; non-language framework IDs return empty JSON), INV-votop (search --kind, --language registry violations — primary face; --limit type-range face is cross-referenced to sub-META B), WI-furop (sketch --require-section silently accepts invalid section names).\n\n**Parent:** INV-fabov-kapit-mupit-tigoz-lurol-mulus-jivik-kajun."  # 86ff
    fields:  # 86ff
      statement: "Every CLI flag whose semantics require a registry lookup (language catalog, framework catalog, section vocabulary, view vocabulary) must reject non-registry values with a helpful did-you-mean hint; no such flag may proceed silently on a non-registry value."  # 86ff
      root_cause: "argparse choices= is not wired through to relevant catalogs at the 5 affected sites. Symptoms: config accepts framework/linker names as if languages (INV-gufod), --input consumers accept wrong-view JSON (INV-gapib), config --format json accepts non-language framework IDs returning empty (INV-subak), search accepts invalid --kind/--language (INV-votop), sketch --require-section accepts invalid section names (WI-furop)."  # 86ff
- op: discuss  # 52c0
  at: '2026-06-02T08:02:21Z'  # 52c0
  by: agent  # 52c0
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 52c0
  clock: 2  # 52c0
  nonce: 52c0  # 52c0
  message: "Pass-32 face: `hypergumbo config <unknown_language>` silently accepts arbitrary language names and returns all-nulls instead of rejecting per argparse `choices=` discipline (F32.6).\n\nINV-murig's scope: \"Every CLI flag whose semantics require a registry lookup (language catalog, framework catalog, section vocabulary, view vocabulary) must reject non-registry values with a helpful did-you-mean hint.\" Pass-32 supplies a `config` subcommand face that complements INV-gufod and INV-subak's existing config-related faces.\n\n**Repro.**\n```\n$ hypergumbo config klingon --format json\n{\n  \"dataflow_patterns\": null,\n  \"io_primitives\": null,\n  \"function_summaries\": null\n}\nWarning: no configuration found for language 'klingon'\n$ echo $?\n0\n```\n\nCompare with:\n```\n$ hypergumbo config python --format json    # exit 0, 19418 bytes of real JSON\n$ hypergumbo config ruby   --format json    # exit 0, real JSON (even though ruby is in limits.skipped_passes for this codebase)\n```\n\nThree observations:\n1. **Exit code is 0** despite the warning. argparse `choices=` would have produced exit 2 with a clear usage message.\n2. **Output is structurally valid JSON** (`{\"dataflow_patterns\": null, \"io_primitives\": null, \"function_summaries\": null}`). A consumer parsing the JSON sees three valid-typed null fields, not an error envelope. The warning to stderr is the only signal that the language is unknown.\n3. **The registry to check against exists.** `hypergumbo catalog` enumerates 117 known language-analyzer passes (`(core)` and `(extra)`); `argparse(... choices=catalog.list_languages())` would have rejected `klingon` at parse time with `error: argument language: invalid choice: 'klingon' (choose from …)`.\n\n**Same-shape members in INV-murig.** INV-gufod (config silently accepts framework/linker names as if they were languages) and INV-subak (config --format json: function_summaries empty for ALL 281 languages). Pass-32 extends the family: not just framework/linker confusion (INV-gufod) and not just an \"all empty\" silent-accept artifact (INV-subak), but **any string at all** is accepted. Together the three faces show the `config` subcommand has no registry-membership gate at any layer.\n\n**INV-fabov's silent-CONFIRM closure (Phase 3 PR4 ClaimVerdict.inconclusive) addressed verify-claims.** The same closure form is needed here: `hypergumbo config <unknown>` should exit-non-zero with a helpful \"did you mean\" suggestion. Currently it exits 0 because the warning is purely informational.\n\n**No status change.** Pass-32 supplies a third `config`-subcommand face under INV-murig demonstrating that the registry-membership gap is broad — beyond INV-gufod (framework/linker confusion) and INV-subak (281-language silent-empty), arbitrary strings are accepted.\n\nProbe artifact: `/tmp/p32_outputB.log` section \"B.7–B.9\". Catalog regex source: `/tmp/p32_catalog.txt` (175 passes / 107 framework patterns / 117 language analyzers enumerated)."  # 52c0
- op: discuss  # 894b
  at: '2026-06-02T17:12:36Z'  # 894b
  by: agent  # 894b
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 894b
  clock: 3  # 894b
  nonce: 894b  # 894b
  message: "Pass-34 batch (4 findings — registry-membership validation gaps at verify-claims + search).\n\n**F34.C1 — verify-claims silently confirms claims with boundary axis values not in the BoundaryMap vocabulary.** Authored an 8-claim YAML using intuitive boundary names: `network`, `process`, `database`, `filesystem`, plus a fictional `banana`. The actual io-boundaries CLI vocabulary (verified via `hypergumbo io-boundaries --json`) is: `env_read`, `external_potential`, `fs_read`, `fs_write`, `ipc_recv`, `logging`, `net_recv`, `net_send`, `subprocess` (9 categories). Intersection with the intuitive names tested: 0. Result for each: `must_not_exist: true` → verdict `confirmed` (because boundary lookup returns None → chain_count=0 → must_not_exist passes the fall-through).\n\n**This codebase actively does network calls (INV-dasig HF Hub access P0 violated) and subprocess.run all over the place — yet `NO_NETWORK_CALLS` (boundary=network) and `NO_SHELL_CALLS` (boundary=process) both confirm.** A user writing claims against intuitive boundary names gets false-confirmations with no way to detect the mismatch.\n\nCode path: `verify_claims.py:236-267` does `entry = boundary_map.entries.get(claim.constraint_boundary)` then `chain_count = len(entry.chains) if entry else 0`. When `entry` is None (boundary value not in BoundaryMap), `chain_count = 0`. Then `must_not_exist` passes silently. This is the same silent-confirm fall-through INV-bitig was meant to fix; Phase 3 PR4's `ClaimVerdict.inconclusive` covered the empty-source-dir case but NOT the boundary-not-in-vocab case.\n\n**F34.C2 — `BOUNDARY_BANANA` (explicitly fictional boundary value) silently confirms** with `details: \"No banana chains found.\"`. The boundary value is never validated against the io-boundaries vocabulary catalog at YAML load time. Cleaner repro than F34.C1 of the same mechanism — INV-murig at the verify-claims boundary axis.\n\n**F34.D2 — `hypergumbo search --kind <invalid>` silently accepts.** Tested `--kind banana`, `--kind FILE` (case mismatch with canonical `file`), `--kind route` (declared kind that exists nowhere in this substrate). All three return `header=0, rc=0, stderr=''`. No \"unknown kind: <X>\" warning; no did-you-mean hint. Same shape as INV-votop's --kind face but more cases. Probe artifact: `/tmp/p34_outputD.log` D.4.\n\n**F34.D4 — `hypergumbo search --language <invalid>` silently accepts.** Tested `--language banana`, `--language PYTHON` (uppercase canonical), `--language unknown`, `--language None`. All return `header=0, rc=0`. Same shape as INV-votop's --language face. The `unknown` literal value is particularly interesting because per pass-25 F25.12, `metrics.languages` includes `unknown` as a key — but `search --language unknown` returns 0.\n\n**Fix-path candidate.** Extend the proposed shared `argparse choices=` wiring + did-you-mean hint mechanism to cover two additional binding sites:\n- `verify-claims --claims` (validate `constraint.boundary` at YAML load time against `boundary-catalog`)\n- `search --kind` and `search --language` (validate at argparse layer against `symbol-kind` and `language` catalogs)\n\nThese are the same shape as INV-votop and WI-furop in the existing member list. Pass-34 grows the member count from 5 to potentially 7+ (verify-claims constraint.boundary + search --kind would be two new members), but the mechanism + fix are identical to the existing pattern.\n\n**Probe artifacts:** `/tmp/p34_claims.yaml`, `/tmp/p34_claims_out.json`, `/tmp/p34_iob.json`, `/tmp/p34_outputD.log` (D.4 + D.5), `/tmp/p34_outputD2.log`. No status change."  # 894b
